// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§18.1", "§2.5"]
// fixes = 0

// (R-396, S-947 (b).) The type is cut and the next line starts with `fn` and a name (or `rt fn` and a name). The
// reading of a type stops at the `fn` (as the reading of an expression does, §18.1: a name after `fn`
// makes it the start of an item), so the `fn` line head ends the unit and the function is read. The unit
// has the one error that is there: the bracket that is never closed (the innermost one, S-948), and the
// users of the function below find it (no E0302).

// ---- a cut that does not continue: the type after `v:` or in the `B(` of a variant

